WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.410
The Elwha River flows north from the
Olympic Mountains to the Strait of Juan de

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.710
Fuca.

3
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.510
Valley glaciers carved
deep U-shaped troughs here;

4
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.450
small glaciers remain
around Mount Olympus.

5
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.010
In 1913, the Elwha Dam rose 32 metres.

6
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:22.970
In 1927, Glines Canyon Dam rose
64 metres, further upstream.

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.770
At the river mouth, the delta
shoreline retreated up to 160 metres,

8
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.150
1939 to 2006.

9
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.090
Did the sea rise faster?

10
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.150
Did storms grow stronger?

11
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.050
Why did the beach at the
river's mouth shrink?

12
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.510
In this mission, you'll
read the Elwha's valley,

13
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.270
from mountain troughs to dams.

14
00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.950
Then you'll find out what
happened when the dams came down,

15
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.110
between 2011 and 2014.

16
00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:54.130
Your mission: explain why the Elwha's
beach shrank while the dams stood.
